<title>FINLAND: NOKIA TO SUPPLY GSM NETWORK TO UZBEKISTAN.</title>
<headline>NOKIA TO SUPPLY GSM NETWORK TO UZBEKISTAN.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-08-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish telecommunications group Nokia Oy said in a statement on Wednesday it won an order to supply a GSM network to Uzbekistan.</p>
<p>Nokia did not give the value of the contract but said deliveries would start in September. In the first phase, the network targets 20,000 subscribers in the first two years, Nokia said.  </p>
<p>The network will be operated by Uzmacom, a joint venture between Uzbekistan Telekom (Uztel) and Superior Communications Sdn.Bdh. of Malaysia, Nokia said.</p>
<p>--Helsinki Newsroom  +358 - 0 - 680 50 245</p>
